CORE broken-smt-backend no-new-smt
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
memcpy with a symbolic size into an array of arrays. Byte-operator lowering
turns this into an array comprehension whose body is an array.
The SMT2 back-end converts the array literal in that body into a separate array
that is constrained outside the lambda, with a free variable in place of the
index of the comprehension. Z3 therefore reports VERIFICATION FAILED, hence
broken-smt-backend. The new SMT back-end fails an invariant (unimplemented
conversion of a tuple expression), hence no-new-smt. --arrays-uf-always also
reports VERIFICATION FAILED, see arrays-uf-always.desc.
